cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Structured Extraction of Echocardiography Reports
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software and the
  accompanying paper.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/ultraub/echo-extraction"

authors:
  - family-names: Barrett
    given-names: Robert B.
    affiliation: >-
      Division of Biomedical Informatics and Data Science, Department of
      Medicine, Johns Hopkins School of Medicine
  - family-names: Duvall
    given-names: Chloe
    affiliation: >-
      Division of Cardiology, Department of Medicine, Johns Hopkins School
      of Medicine
  - family-names: Hays
    given-names: Allison G.
    affiliation: >-
      Division of Cardiology, Department of Medicine, Johns Hopkins School
      of Medicine
  - family-names: Minhas
    given-names: Anum S.
    affiliation: >-
      Division of Cardiology, Department of Medicine, Johns Hopkins School
      of Medicine

abstract: >-
  A fine-tuning-free pipeline that extracts 48 structured clinical fields
  from free-text echocardiography reports using a general-purpose large
  language model with JSON-schema-constrained decoding. Runs against a
  locally self-hosted open-weights model or any OpenAI-compatible endpoint.

keywords:
  - echocardiography
  - clinical natural language processing
  - information extraction
  - large language models
  - structured data

